{
  "schema": 1,
  "title": "How one context window carries a whole round",
  "mechanism": "The orchestrator hands each task to a child session with a window of its own and takes back one line, so its own window fills slowly.",
  "lens": "time",
  "claim": "A window that delegates holds hand-offs and one-line reports, not the work, so a 500K threshold is room for a whole round.",
  "implication": "Set auto-compaction to 500K tokens or less: the hook brings the instructions back, and the board brings back the round.",
