      "plain": "A second child starts beside the first, and a child starts a helper of its own.",
      "technical": "Cards whose files are disjoint run in parallel; a child's subagent gets the critical lines marked for every agent."
    },
    {
      "id": "talk",
      "title": "They coordinate",
      "ms": 3000,
      "focus": [
        "child-a",
        "child-b"
      ],
      "flows": [
        "note"
      ],
      "plain": "Sessions leave each other notes, so one learns what another changed without the orchestrator relaying it.",
      "technical": "aw note writes one line to the project's notes log, which every worktree shares; aw notes reads it."
    },
    {
      "id": "report",
      "title": "One line comes back",
      "ms": 3200,
      "focus": [
        "child-a",
        "orchestrator"
      ],
      "flows": [
        "report"
      ],
      "plain": "The child's whole task returns as a single line, so the orchestrator's window grows by a few rows per task.",
      "technical": "The first line of the child's final message is the CARD line: only the start of a report is quoted back."
    },
